EXPLAIN YOUR MOST CHALLENGING PROJECT: FARM MARKETPLACE


Farm Marketplace is my final-year project and one of the most challenging projects I have worked on because it combines multiple areas of technology and addresses a real-world problem.

The main problem we wanted to address is the difficulty farmers can face in directly reaching buyers. In a traditional supply chain, there can be multiple intermediaries between farmers and customers. Our objective is to build a digital marketplace where farmers can list their agricultural products and connect more directly with buyers.

The platform is designed around multiple users, mainly farmers, buyers, and delivery partners. Farmers can list their products, buyers can browse and place orders, and delivery partners can handle the logistics side.

One of the interesting parts of the project is the AI agent concept. The purpose of the AI component is to assist with organizing and managing order-related activities. We are also exploring a blockchain-based trust layer to improve transparency and trust in certain transactions or records.

From a technical perspective, the challenging part is not just building individual features, but integrating multiple components into one system. We have to think about user roles, order management, communication between the application and backend, data storage, delivery workflows, and how the AI and blockchain components can add real value instead of simply being included as technologies.

The biggest learning from this project has been understanding that a real-world application is not only about writing code. It requires good system design, clear responsibilities, integration between components, handling real user workflows, and making practical technology decisions.

Going forward, we want to further improve the platform's reliability, scalability, AI capabilities, and trust mechanisms based on real user requirements.


